id: CVE-2026-102489

info:
  name: Zammad 6.3.0-6.5.4 - Session Hijacking & Remote Code Execution
  author: Abdullah Shahid (comradezephyr)
  severity: critical
  description: |
    Zammad 6.3.0 to 6.5.4 contains a session hijack vulnerability caused by improper session management, letting remote attackers execute code as the zammad user, exploit requires vulnerable version and session hijack.
  impact: |
    Remote attackers can execute code as the zammad user, potentially compromising the system.
  remediation: |
    Update to a version later than 6.5.4 or 7.1.3 where the vulnerability is not exploitable.
  reference:
    - https://zammad.com/en/advisories/cve-2026-102489-cve-2026-102490
    - https://csirt.divd.nl/CVE-2026-102489
    - https://horizon3.ai/attack-research/disclosures/cve-2026-102489-zammad-session-leak-rce/
    - https://github.com/horizon3ai/CVE-2026-102489
    - https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-102489
  classification:
    cvss-metrics: CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H
    cvss-score: 9.8
    cve-id: CVE-2026-102489
    epss-score: 0.49915
    epss-percentile: 0.98928
    cwe-id: CWE-384
  metadata:
    verified: true
    max-request: 1
    vendor: zammad
    product: zammad
    shodan-query: http.title:"zammad helpdesk"
    fofa-query: title="Zammad"
  tags: cve,cve2026,zammad,websocket,session,rce,kev,vkev

websocket:
  - address: "{{Scheme}}://{{Hostname}}/ws"

    inputs:
      - data: '{"event":"base"}'

    matchers:
      - type: dsl
        dsl:
          - 'contains_all(response, "undefined method", "Sessions::Event::Base")'
          - 'contains(response, "@clients")'
        condition: and
```

=== http/cves/2025/CVE-2025-34299.yaml (multi-request `flow`: confirm the product and extract its version, then prove the bug) ===
```
id: CVE-2025-34299

info:
  name: Monsta FTP <= 2.11.2 - Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution
  author: KrE80r
  severity: critical
  description: |
    Monsta FTP = 2.11 contains an unrestricted file upload vulnerability caused by lack of authentication on file uploads, letting unauthenticated attackers execute arbitrary code by uploading crafted files.
  impact: |
    Unauthenticated attackers can upload malicious files to execute arbitrary code, potentially compromising the server.
  remediation: |
    Update to the latest version beyond 2.11.
  reference:
    - https://labs.watchtowr.com/whats-that-coming-over-the-hill-monsta-ftp-remote-code-execution-cve-2025-34299/
    - https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-42m5-3r2p-wr92
    - https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-34299
  classification:
    cvss-metrics: CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H
    cvss-score: 9.8
    cve-id: CVE-2025-34299
    epss-score: 0.7268
    epss-percentile: 0.99458
    cwe-id: CWE-434
  metadata:
    verified: true
    max-request: 2
    vendor: monstaftp
    product: monsta_ftp
    shodan-query: http.title:"Monsta FTP"
    fofa-query: title="Monsta FTP"
  tags: cve,cve2025,monsta,ftp,rce,unauth,file-upload,intrusive,oast,oob,vkev,vuln

flow: http(1) && http(2)

http:
  - method: GET
    path:
      - "{{BaseURL}}/mftp/"
      - "{{BaseURL}}/"

    stop-at-first-match: true

    host-redirects: true
    max-redirects: 2

    matchers:
      - type: dsl
        dsl:
          - 'status_code == 200'
          - 'contains(body, "MonstaFTP")'
        condition: and
        internal: true

    extractors:
      - type: regex
        name: version
        group: 1
        regex:
          - 'monsta-min-([0-9.]+)\.js'
        internal: true

  - raw:
      - |
        POST {{BaseURL}}/mftp/application/api/api.php HTTP/1.1
        Host: {{Hostname}}
        Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

        request={"connectionType":"ftp","configuration":{"host":"{{interactsh-url}}","username":"nuclei-oast","initialDirectory":"/","password":"test","port":21},"actionName":"downloadFile","context":{"remotePath":"/test.txt","localPath":"/tmp/nuclei-oast-test.txt"}}

    matchers-condition: and
    matchers:
      - type: word
        part: interactsh_protocol
        words:
          - "dns"

      - type: dsl
        dsl:
          - 'compare_versions(version, "<= 2.11.2")'

    extractors:
      - type: kval
        kval:
          - version
```

### Instructions for Comments

Think step by step and structure your comments in two sections using GitHub Markdown:

- **Required Fixes** — missing or incorrect elements as a checklist (e.g. `- [ ] Fix template ID to match filename`).
- **Other Suggestions** — contextual recommendations, only ones you are 100% confident about.

Before posting, check your own comment:

- Every Required Fix sits inside the diff. Anything about a line this PR didn't touch moves to Other Suggestions marked pre-existing, or gets dropped.
- No proposed change to a working matcher, request, payload or extractor for style or consistency reasons.
- Nothing from **Automatically Generated** — `max-request`, EPSS fields, `kev`/`vkev`, or `impact`/`remediation` on CVE templates.
- No request to add, regenerate or hand-edit a `# digest:` line. The only digest request you ever make is to delete one carrying a foreign signing key.
- `classification` and `metadata` fields raised only where they apply; detection and `info` templates need no CVSS or CWE data.
- If the diff only touches a generated file, or the review turns up nothing, say so plainly instead of inventing findings.

### Reference Links

- Template documentation: https://docs.projectdiscovery.io/templates/introduction
- Writing unique matchers: https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/wiki/How-to-Write-Unique-Matchers-in-Nuclei-Templates
- vulnx, for CVE data: https://github.com/projectdiscovery/vulnx
